  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f974ebb5cd41de74683ff3a0eb9cb068, type: 3}
  m_Name: Lore-en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 
  text: 'In 1996, the air in Harrow Creek was thick with terror. The "Harrow Creek
    Butcher" wasn''t a legend, but a real killer, staining the town with blood. His
    macabre calling card: a kitchen knife plunged into the chest of his victims.


    Ethan
    Myers, a young reporter hungry for the truth, plunged headfirst into the case''s
    darkness.


    Then, in a chilling silence, the Butcher vanished. No body, no
    confession. The town never knew if he died... or simply went into hiding. The
    shadow of his knife still hangs over the city.


    The cost of that investigation
    tore Ethan Myers''s mind apart. Years passed, but Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder
    (PTSD) holds him captive.


    At any moment, the real world shatters. His vision
    darkens, the air turns hostile, and the terror of 1996 crawls back.


    The
    only barrier between Ethan and total madness is medication. He must remain medicated,
    fighting daily to keep the monster he once covered from consuming him from the
    inside.'
